Based on this analysis, there is a fairly wide confidence interval around the median, in this case it is between 1.41 and `r(round(quans[2], 2))`. This gives a range of plausible values for the population median, based on our sample.

Normally, this would be our end point, but, in this case, we do have a better estimate of the population median. In this dataset, relatively few (85) organisms had data for all our traits of interest, but 917 had data for at least iron concentration. This data is provided as `data/inverts_iron.csv`. This data will not provide a population median, but it can give us a more estimate of the population median than our 85 organism sample.

